+	// Texture replacement (BT2 Recomp patch): called when a texture is about to be cached from VRAM.
+	// A non-null image is used instead: it holds the whole 2^TW x 2^TH texture at any resolution, in a
+	// block-compressed format (which marks it as a replacement), and is sampled with the texture's own
+	// coordinates. Textures with super-samples are never replaced.
+	std::function<Vulkan::ImageHandle (const TextureDescriptor &)> texture_replacement;
+
